  "scope": "The three cat wires control P2, P1 and P0 on their corresponding data wires in source order. The native circuit records all three X-basis ancilla measurements and computes their XOR. Authored readouts measure the data in the indicated bases.",
  "reference": "Each parity projector is (I + (-1)^s P)/2, shared equally among four cat readout words. An X component of a fault on a prepared cat qubit propagates its controlled Pauli to its one data target. A Z component flips the parity. Cases use complementary data readouts to distinguish both effects.",
  "limits": "Faults are inserted after ideal cat preparation and before the controlled gates. Cat verification, noisy preparation and threshold behavior are outside these cases.",
  "exact_cases": 26,
  "sampled_cases": 26,
  "shots_per_case": 10000,
  "bit_order": "Computed parity, three ancilla bits (5,4,3), then three data bits (2,1,0).",
